        "original_id": "d5ff2f2b-5167-5b1d-848c-def3d264ae69",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Greater Swiss Mountain Dog, Hanover Hound\n- Places: Swiss Alps, Switzerland\n- Concepts: dog breed origins, hunting and tracking dogs, medieval bloodhounds, dog show rankings\n\nFacts:\n- The Greater Swiss Mountain Dog is a dog breed developed in the Swiss Alps.\n- The Greater Swiss Mountain Dog almost certainly resulted from indigenous dogs mating with large mastiff types brought to Switzerland by foreign settlers.\n- The Hanover Hound is a breed of dog also called the Hanoverian Hound.\n- The Hanover Hound is a hunting and tracking dog descended from medieval bloodhounds.\n- Oscar the Grouch is a top-ranked Greater Swiss Mountain Dog that was seen on opening promos for the Dog Show on USA Network and on Bloomberg.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "bf287f5c-2d40-5f6b-aa0e-9b5fdba298e7",
        "text": "Page: Greater Swiss Mountain Dog. Sentence: The Greater Swiss Mountain Dog (German: \"Grosser Schweizer Sennenhund\" or French: \"Grand Bouvier Suisse\" ) is a dog breed which was developed in the Swiss Alps.\nPage: Greater Swiss Mountain Dog. Sentence: Greater Swiss Mountain Dogs are almost certainly the result of indigenous dogs mating with large mastiff types brought to Switzerland by foreign settlers.\nPage: Hanover Hound. Sentence: The Hanover Hound is a breed of dog sometimes referred to as a Hanoverian Hound.\nPage: Hanover Hound. Sentence: It is a hunting and tracking dog descended from bloodhounds of medieval times.\nPage: Oscar the Grouch (dog). Sentence: Also seen on the opening promo for the Dog Show on the USA Network and on Bloomberg, Oscar is a top-ranked Greater Swiss Mountain Dog.",
